<%#
  SOL → USD cost calculator. Editable SOL price; recomputes the
  permanent + refundable + total-float costs in dollars. The lamport lines do
  not depend on the SOL price, so they render server-side from the measured
  figures; Alpine only drives the SOL/USD totals.

  EVERY LAMPORT FIGURE HERE IS QUERIED, NOT MULTIPLIED. The *_min locals come
  from getMinimumBalanceForRentExemption at measured[:slot]; the *_balance
  locals are what the live accounts hold. They differ because the two were
  priced at different rates, and this block keeps them apart.
    locals: deployed_file_bytes, programdata_space, buffer_space, program_acct_space,
            pd_rent_min, buffer_rent_min, program_acct_min, programdata_balance,
            program_acct_balance, funded_rate, current_rate, measured

  Alpine factory lives in the parent show.html.erb (window.contractCostCalculator)
  because the factory MUST be defined inline before Alpine processes x-data
  (importmap modules load too late — feedback_alpine_factory_importmap_timing).
%>
<section class="card p-6 sm:p-8 mb-6" x-data="contractCostCalculator()">
  <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-baseline sm:gap-4 mb-2">
    <h2 class="text-heading font-bold text-xl">Deploy-cost calculator</h2>
    <span class="text-[11px] font-mono text-muted uppercase tracking-wider">SOL &rarr; USD</span>
  </div>
  <p class="text-secondary text-sm mb-5 max-w-3xl" data-test="contract-rent-rate-copy">
    An account is rent-exempt once it holds the minimum for its size, and that minimum is
    <em>not</em> a fixed constant &mdash; the cluster sets the per-byte rate and has been lowering it.
    Ask the chain rather than multiply:
    <code class="font-mono bg-surface-alt px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">solana rent <%= programdata_space %></code>,
    or <code class="font-mono bg-surface-alt px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded text-xs">getMinimumBalanceForRentExemption</code>.
    Every minimum below was queried at slot <%= number_with_delimiter(measured[:slot]) %> (<%= measured[:date] %>),
    where it worked out to <%= number_with_delimiter(current_rate) %> lamports a byte.
    This program's accounts were funded at <%= number_with_delimiter(funded_rate) %>, so what they hold
    is more than what they would cost to open today.
  </p>

  <%# Live readouts row — wraps to new lines on mobile %>
  <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3 sm:gap-5 mb-5 text-sm">
    <label class="flex items-center gap-2 text-secondary">
      <span>SOL price:</span>
      <span class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 bg-surface-alt rounded px-2 py-1 border border-subtle">
        <span class="text-muted">$</span>
        <input type="number" min="1" max="10000" step="1" x-model.number="solPrice"
               class="bg-transparent border-none outline-none w-20 font-mono text-heading tabular-nums text-sm">
      </span>
    </label>
    <span class="font-mono text-secondary text-xs sm:text-sm">
      Deployed file: <strong class="text-heading tabular-nums"><%= number_with_delimiter(deployed_file_bytes) %></strong> bytes
    </span>
    <span class="font-mono text-secondary text-xs sm:text-sm">
      SOL needed: <strong class="text-primary tabular-nums" x-text="fmtSol(floatSol)">--</strong>
    </span>
    <span class="font-mono text-secondary text-xs sm:text-sm">
      &asymp; <strong class="text-heading tabular-nums" x-text="fmtUsd(floatUsd)">--</strong>
    </span>
  </div>

  <%# Two side-by-side breakdown blocks %>
  <div class="grid gap-4 lg:grid-cols-2">

    <%# Permanent block — what you spend forever %>
    <div class="bg-surface-alt rounded-lg border border-subtle p-4 sm:p-5">
      <h3 class="text-heading font-semibold text-sm mb-3">PERMANENT (you spend forever)</h3>
      <dl class="space-y-1.5 font-mono text-xs sm:text-[13px] text-secondary">
        <div class="flex justify-between items-baseline gap-2">
          <dt class="truncate" data-test="contract-pd-rent-min-line" data-space="<%= programdata_space %>">ProgramData minimum, <%= number_with_delimiter(programdata_space) %> bytes</dt>
          <dd class="text-heading tabular-nums whitespace-nowrap" data-test="contract-pd-rent-min"><%= number_with_delimiter(pd_rent_min) %> &#8467;</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="flex justify-between items-baseline gap-2">
          <dt class="truncate" data-space="<%= program_acct_space %>">Program account minimum, <%= number_with_delimiter(program_acct_space) %> bytes</dt>
          <dd class="text-heading tabular-nums whitespace-nowrap" data-test="contract-program-acct-min"><%= number_with_delimiter(program_acct_min) %> &#8467;</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="flex justify-between items-baseline gap-2">
          <dt class="truncate">Deploy TX fees (signatures + compute)</dt>
          <dd class="text-heading tabular-nums whitespace-nowrap" data-test="contract-tx-fee">1,000,000 &#8467;</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="flex justify-between items-baseline gap-2 pt-2 mt-2 border-t border-subtle">
          <dt class="text-heading font-semibold">Permanent SOL at that slot's rate</dt>
          <dd class="text-warning tabular-nums font-semibold whitespace-nowrap" x-text="'~' + fmtSol(permSol) + ' SOL'">--</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="flex justify-between items-baseline gap-2">
          <dt class="text-muted">&asymp; at current price</dt>
          <dd class="text-heading tabular-nums whitespace-nowrap" x-text="'~' + fmtUsd(permUsd)">--</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="flex justify-between items-baseline gap-2 pt-2 mt-2 border-t border-subtle">
          <dt class="text-secondary">What this program's accounts hold today</dt>
          <dd class="text-heading tabular-nums whitespace-nowrap" data-test="contract-accounts-balance"><%= number_with_delimiter(programdata_balance + program_acct_balance) %> &#8467;</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="flex justify-between items-baseline gap-2">
          <dt class="text-muted">&mdash; funded at <%= number_with_delimiter(funded_rate) %> lamports a byte, not today's <%= number_with_delimiter(current_rate) %></dt>
          <dd></dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>

    <%# Float block — what you need on hand, then refundable %>
    <div class="bg-surface-alt rounded-lg border border-subtle p-4 sm:p-5">
      <h3 class="text-heading font-semibold text-sm mb-3">FLOAT (you need on hand, then refundable)</h3>
      <dl class="space-y-1.5 font-mono text-xs sm:text-[13px] text-secondary">
        <div class="flex justify-between items-baseline gap-2">
          <dt class="truncate" data-test="contract-buffer-min-line" data-space="<%= buffer_space %>">Buffer minimum, <%= number_with_delimiter(buffer_space) %> bytes (37 + the <%= number_with_delimiter(deployed_file_bytes) %>-byte file)</dt>
          <dd class="text-heading tabular-nums whitespace-nowrap" data-test="contract-buffer-min"><%= number_with_delimiter(buffer_rent_min) %> &#8467;</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="flex justify-between items-baseline">
          <dt class="text-muted">&mdash; refunded when you close the buffer</dt>
          <dd></dd>
        </div>
        <div class="flex justify-between items-baseline gap-2 pt-2 mt-2 border-t border-subtle">
          <dt class="text-heading font-semibold">Additional float during deploy</dt>
          <dd class="text-mint tabular-nums font-semibold whitespace-nowrap" x-text="'~' + fmtSol(bufferSol) + ' SOL'">--</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="flex justify-between items-baseline gap-2">
          <dt class="text-muted">&asymp; at current price</dt>
          <dd class="text-heading tabular-nums whitespace-nowrap" x-text="'~' + fmtUsd(bufferUsd)">--</dd>
        </div>
        <div class="flex justify-between items-baseline gap-2 pt-2 mt-2 border-t border-subtle">
          <dt class="text-secondary">Recommended balance before write-buffer</dt>
          <dd class="text-primary tabular-nums font-semibold whitespace-nowrap" x-text="'~' + fmtSol(floatSol) + ' SOL'">--</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>

  </div>

  <p class="text-secondary text-[13px] mt-5 max-w-3xl leading-relaxed">
    Subsequent upgrades through the Squad multisig need only the <em>float</em> portion &mdash; a new
    buffer is written, the program is upgraded in place, then the old buffer is closed.
    Net cost per upgrade: roughly zero, modulo TX fees and the brief float for the new buffer.
  </p>
</section>
